def find_max(lst):
    if not lst:
        raise ValueError('List is empty')
    maximum = lst[0]
    for item in lst:
        if item > maximum:
            maximum = item
    return maximum

# Example
find_max([3, 1, 7, 2, 9, 4])  # 9
```

This iterates through the list once, tracking the largest value seen so far. Time complexity is O(n) — linear in the size of the list.

